WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:29.166 --> 00:00:31.375
After spending two days
in Kinosaki Onsen,

00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:32.875
we head towards Kyoto

00:00:33.416 --> 00:00:35.875
to spend the next five days
exploring the city,

00:00:36.041 --> 00:00:37.750
along with a day trip to Nara.

00:00:45.583 --> 00:00:47.958
All right, we just arrived in Kyoto

00:00:48.458 --> 00:00:51.125
and yeah, arrived quite late.

00:00:51.625 --> 00:00:54.916
So now we're just out on the prowl
to get some dinner

00:00:55.041 --> 00:00:58.791
and I know just the right place
for us tonight.

00:00:59.083 --> 00:01:00.958
So let's head in.

00:03:00.250 --> 00:03:02.791
We are very close to the
top of Mount Inari

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:06.958
and honestly, not as bad as I thought.

00:03:06.958 --> 00:03:08.583
I thought it would be a bit tougher,

00:03:09.708 --> 00:03:13.166
but once you get up to the
crossroad area,

00:03:13.583 --> 00:03:16.125
people start to thin out and
you get a lot of photo

00:03:16.833 --> 00:03:18.958
and video opportunities if that's
what you're looking for.

00:03:19.416 --> 00:03:21.791
Definitely recommend taking the walk up.

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:22.875
It's really not that bad.

00:03:22.875 --> 00:03:26.500
Just take your time and you should
be just all right.

00:03:51.458 --> 00:03:53.583
All right, I'm making my way
down Mount Inari

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:58.541
and towards Kyoto and a little bit later

00:03:58.750 --> 00:04:01.875
our restaurant reservation.

00:04:02.500 --> 00:04:05.416
Look at this, an Aquarius is ¥250.

00:04:05.541 --> 00:04:08.458
That is the mountain tax in effect.

00:04:09.625 --> 00:04:11.458
Usually like ¥150 or something like that.

00:04:11.833 --> 00:04:12.583
Yep, mountain tax.

00:04:13.416 --> 00:04:15.416
If you can make it, make
it down the mountain

00:04:16.375 --> 00:04:17.250
and avoid the mountain tax.

00:04:17.791 --> 00:04:18.291
Look at this guys.

00:04:18.625 --> 00:04:19.416
Look at this, look at this.

00:04:19.708 --> 00:04:22.125
The lower you get, the lower
the price also becomes.

00:04:22.125 --> 00:04:23.541
The mountain tax is less.

00:04:24.458 --> 00:04:25.416
This is the Pocari Sweat.

00:04:41.625 --> 00:04:43.625
After finishing up at Fushimi Inari,

00:04:44.166 --> 00:04:45.583
we head to our dinner reservation

00:04:45.958 --> 00:04:47.125
at Mouriya Gion,

00:04:47.500 --> 00:04:50.625
a teppanyaki restaurant 
specialized in Kobe beef.

00:04:53.375 --> 00:04:55.708
The menu consisted of 
a couple of starters,

00:04:56.791 --> 00:04:58.083
including flounder fish.

00:05:00.833 --> 00:05:04.416
This is flounder fish and so this
is Japan's green pepper "sansho"

00:05:04.416 --> 00:05:06.541
butter, white wine
and white vinegar.

00:05:07.375 --> 00:05:09.625
But the main event is 
the A5 Kobe beef.

00:05:10.625 --> 00:05:11.958
The preparation was meticulous

00:05:12.541 --> 00:05:14.125
and it was interesting 
to watch the chef

00:05:14.291 --> 00:05:15.833
prepare the beef right in front of us.

00:05:54.208 --> 00:05:56.125
We end the dinner with a simple dessert

00:05:57.625 --> 00:05:58.833
and some hot tea.

00:07:31.125 --> 00:07:33.291
The following morning 
we head to Arashiyama

00:07:33.750 --> 00:07:35.458
to explore some of its quieter corners.

00:08:37.875 --> 00:08:39.375
As lunch time rolls around,

00:08:39.833 --> 00:08:42.166
we stop by a place 
called Itsuki Chaya,

00:08:42.875 --> 00:08:46.000
a restaurant known for its 
beautifully prepared set meals

00:08:46.333 --> 00:08:48.166
that highlight seasonal ingredients.

00:09:00.083 --> 00:09:01.125
Are you hungry?

00:09:01.291 --> 00:09:02.083
I'm hungry too.

00:09:52.083 --> 00:09:55.583
We also made sure to make
room for a little visit to Kumonocha,

00:09:55.875 --> 00:09:58.958
a small dessert shop known for 
its cloud shaped cakes.

00:12:11.166 --> 00:12:13.333
After spending the morning visiting temples,

00:12:13.333 --> 00:12:15.083
we head back to downtown Kyoto

00:12:15.333 --> 00:12:17.083
and stop by Nishiki Market.

00:12:42.916 --> 00:12:43.625
Is it good?

00:12:44.250 --> 00:12:44.750
It's fat.

00:13:01.708 --> 00:13:04.041
where do we go, 
where do we go.

00:13:07.500 --> 00:13:09.416
Give him a chance to clean up for you

00:13:31.875 --> 00:13:32.750
So good.

00:13:52.250 --> 00:13:53.541
Very, very chewy.

00:13:54.791 --> 00:13:56.125
I do not recommend this.

00:14:52.500 --> 00:14:55.750
The next morning, we visited 
a beautiful tea house

00:14:56.166 --> 00:15:01.500
known for their clear Hanawarabi, 
a type of clear mochi with edible flowers.

00:15:50.416 --> 00:15:53.833
After the tea house, we head down
to the Higashiyama area

00:15:54.333 --> 00:15:56.750
and explore the city's old historic district.

00:17:18.750 --> 00:17:21.583
All right, we are at the Nijo Castle.

00:17:21.583 --> 00:17:26.625
And as you can see, it's very dark, 
except for some light illuminations

00:17:26.625 --> 00:17:28.083
around the castle because we're at,

00:17:28.083 --> 00:17:30.875
I believe it's called 
the Naked Sakura Festival.

00:17:31.333 --> 00:17:33.708
Essentially, they're lighting up Nijo Castle

00:17:33.708 --> 00:17:36.458
with some light illuminations, 
kind of like team Labs I guess,

00:17:36.458 --> 00:17:39.375
is the closest thing I would 
compare it to, but yeah.

00:17:39.708 --> 00:17:42.708
Yeah, and we also rented these lanterns.

00:18:31.416 --> 00:18:33.250
Alright, we are on a day trip to...

00:18:35.208 --> 00:18:39.208
And first stop is a pretty
famous mochi place.

00:18:39.416 --> 00:18:41.541
You've probably seen it all
over social media.

00:18:59.500 --> 00:19:00.833
Classic red bean.

00:19:01.541 --> 00:19:02.125
It's good.

00:19:02.250 --> 00:19:03.083
It's a little bit cold.

00:19:03.458 --> 00:19:06.208
I wish it was a little bit warmer.

00:19:06.458 --> 00:19:07.500
It's still alright, you know.

00:19:07.666 --> 00:19:09.666
But lots of people right now.

00:19:09.708 --> 00:19:12.583
So maybe we'll circle back later.

00:21:17.625 --> 00:21:20.583
Just waiting for Lisa to get up here.

00:21:21.000 --> 00:21:21.791
Here she comes.

00:21:23.125 --> 00:21:24.041
Taking her time.

00:21:25.958 --> 00:21:26.458
All good.

00:22:36.541 --> 00:22:37.250
Are you hungry?

00:22:38.541 --> 00:22:39.833
Hungry, hungry, hungry...

00:23:40.083 --> 00:23:41.708
On our final evening in the city,

00:23:42.291 --> 00:23:43.791
we make our way to the old district,

00:23:44.250 --> 00:23:46.125
wandering its lantern-lit streets.

00:23:58.833 --> 00:24:02.458
We came across a special evening event 
at Kiyomizu-dera

00:24:02.750 --> 00:24:05.041
that only occurs three times a year.

